## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical incident response design, Azure Key Vault integrations, and rollback discipline using beginner-friendly tooling.

## Key Concepts
- Incident response workflow
- Azure Key Vault secret rotation
- Managed Identities for AAD auth
- Event Grid / Gateways for triggering automation
- Rollback strategy with last-known-good secret

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-rotate-secret workflow (illustrative)
async function rotateSecret(vault, name) {
  const newValue = generateSecret();
  await vault.setSecret({ name, value: newValue });
  // notify apps to refresh
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rotation success without downtime?
- What monitoring alerts would you add to detect rotation failures?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests incident-response planning across Defender for Cloud, Azure AD, Key Vault, and cross-subscription governance.

## Key Concepts
- Automated incident response playbooks
- Key Vault secret rotation
- Managed identities and service principals
- Canary rollouts and rollback strategies
- Cross-subscription isolation and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Rotate secret using Node.js Azure SDK
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');
const vault = new SecretClient(`https://${'ProdKV'}.vault.azure.net`, new DefaultAzureCredential());
async function rotate(){ const newVal = require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64');
  await vault.setSecret('dbPassword', newVal);
}
rotate().catch(console.error);
```
